  "text_content": "Menu Student Files Classes Instructor Open submenu Reports Open submenu Set Class Schedule School Permits Close submenu Instructor Instructor Schedule Open submenu Instructor Reports Open submenu My Signatures Close submenu Instructor Schedule Booked Appointments Specify Hours Close submenu Instructor Reports Work Summary To Do Lists Close submenu Reports AQTR Registrations Ilan Preisler logout Self-Evaluation of In-Car Session Practical Session #5 Zhang, Xinyi 1. In the Learner's view, what are the strengths and what are the weaknesses to be worked on at this stage of he practical training? S: control of car, speed, turns, W: looking ahead, blind spot checks, staring at car in front, 2. In the Instructor's view, what are the strengths and what are the weaknesses to be worked on at this stage of he practical training? Agree with student. Good control of car. To work on lifting eyes up and scanning further ahead. This will give you more time to analyze the situation and come up with a plan of action. Ensure mirrors are checked every 5-10 seconds. Try to practice more on multi-lane roadways and in denser traffic. Student Student Signature Zhang, Xinyi Jan 31, 2026 Instructor Instructor Signature Tze L L12618 Save",
